    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="1214" n="1118" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1118"/>

                <head>No. 755.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Stenersen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 10,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 25th ultimo, renewing the request made by you on the 2d of
                    October, 1872, that the line of steamers plying between Norway and the United
                        <pb facs="1215" n="1119" xml:id="pg1119"/> States may be favored with the
                    same exemption from payment, in this country, of tonnage, anchorage, beaconage,
                    and light-house dues that has been granted to the Belgian steamers in virtue of
                    the treaty between the United States and Belgium of July 17, 1858, and to obtain
                    the restitution of the duties which have already been paid.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to state that the question will again be referred to
                    the Secretary of the Treasury for his consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
